Journey: Renewal reminders and claim deadlines follow the calendar (fake clock)
Id: dates-on-fake-clock
Tags: @portal @dates @clock @regression
Role: policyholder
Risk: 4
Requirements: PORTAL-3, FNOL-4
Clock: fixed 2026-12-20 10:00 Europe/London
Description: The browser's clock is frozen on 20 December 2026, so the date rules are tested on the dates that matter, then moved on past the policy's end date.

Log in
Open /app/home
  Expect the page contains "Today is 2026-12-20."
# Expectations computed from the same (fake) today
Set variable renewsIn to daysBetween(today(), "2026-12-31")
Expect ${renewsIn} == 11
Expect testid=renewal-POL-H-100231 has text "Policy POL-H-100231 renews in ${renewsIn} days (on 2026-12-31)."
Expect the page does not contain "Policy POL-M-200455 renews"

# Claim deadlines: 30 days from the incident, late after that, never in the future
Click the "Make a claim" link
  Expect the page contains "Make a claim"
Select "POL-H-100231 - Home" from @ClaimForm.policy
Set variable lateIncident to format(addDays(today(), -40), "YYYY-MM-DD")
Fill @ClaimForm.incidentDate with ${lateIncident}
  Expect @ClaimForm.dateNote has text "Late notification: this incident happened 40 days ago. Claims reported more than 30 days after the incident take longer to assess."
Set variable recentIncident to format(addDays(today(), -5), "YYYY-MM-DD")
Set variable deadline to format(addDays(recentIncident, 30), "YYYY-MM-DD")
Fill @ClaimForm.incidentDate with ${recentIncident}
  Expect @ClaimForm.dateNote has text "Reporting deadline: ${deadline} (25 days left)."
Fill @ClaimForm.incidentDate with 2026-12-24
  Expect @ClaimForm.dateNote has text "The incident date cannot be in the future."

# Time moves on: after the end date the policy is shown as expired
Set the clock to 2027-01-04 09:00
Click the "Home" link
  Expect the page contains "Today is 2027-01-04."
Expect the page contains "Policy POL-H-100231 expired on 2026-12-31. Renew it to stay covered."
